A Blazor component (.razor) subscribes to an event on a Singleton 'AppState' service:

@inject AppState State
@code {
    protected override void OnInitialized() {
        State.OnBalanceChanged += () => InvokeAsync(StateHasChanged);
    }
}

MANDATORY REQUIREMENTS:
Explain the root cause of the Memory Leak based on object Lifetimes: why a long-lived 'Singleton' service maintains a 'Strong Reference' to the short-lived Blazor component instance via the delegate. Show the solution by implementing '@implements IDisposable' and unsubscribing from the event.

A Blazor component in Static Server-Side Rendering (SSR) mode loads a product list from the database:

@page "/products"
@inject ProductService Svc

@if (_products == null) {
    <p>Loading...</p>
} else {
    @foreach (var p in _products) { <ProductCard Product="p" /> }
}

@code {
    private List<Product>? _products;
    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync() {
        _products = await Svc.GetAllAsync();
    }
}

The user sees a blank page for 2 seconds before any content is displayed.
MANDATORY REQUIREMENTS:
1. Explain the limitation of Static SSR without streaming: the server completes all rendering before sending the initial HTML bytes to the client.
2. Add '@attribute [StreamRendering]' and show how the component sends placeholder HTML ('Loading...') immediately, then updates the DOM once data becomes available.

